  "reached": false,
  "correct": false
 },
 {
  "id": "pymatgen#8",
  "skill": "pymatgen",
  "cond": "none",
  "answer": "Use pymatgen.analysis.local_env.CrystalNN; call get_nn_info(structure, 0). Its length gives the coordination number and its entries include neighbor distances. For CN only, use get_cn(structure, 0).",
  "opened": [],
  "chars": 0,
  "reached": false,
  "correct": true
 },
 {
  "id": "pymatgen#9",
  "skill": "pymatgen",
  "cond": "none",
  "answer": "Use DFT total energies to construct the Li–Fe–O convex hull (e.g., pymatgen/Materials Project); energy above hull = E(LiFeO2) − E(hull). It is stable if ≈0 eV/atom (within ~1 meV/atom); decomposition is indicated when >0, typically >~1 meV/atom.",
  "opened": [],
  "chars": 0,
  "reached": false,
  "correct": true
 },
 {
  "id": "pymatgen#10",
  "skill": "pymatgen",
  "cond": "none",
  "answer": "Use vasprun.get_band_structure() to get a BandStructure; then bs.get_band_gap() returns {'energy': gap, 'direct': bool, ...}, and bs.is_metal() returns whether it is metallic. Also bs.get_direct_band_gap() gives the direct gap if needed.",
  "opened": [],
  "chars": 0,
  "reached": false,
  "correct": true
 },
 {
  "id": "pymatgen#11",
  "skill": "pymatgen",
  "cond": "none",
  "answer": "Use pymatgen.core.surface.SlabGenerator(structure, (1,1,1), min_slab_size=10, min_vacuum_size=10, center_slab=True), then call .get_slab().",
  "opened": [],
  "chars": 0,
  "reached": false,
  "correct": true
 },
 {
  "id": "pymatgen#12",
  "skill": "pymatgen",
  "cond": "none",
  "answer": "Instantiate pymatgen.analysis.adsorption.AdsorbateSiteFinder(slab), then call find_adsorption_sites(); it returns the on-top, bridge, and hollow sites.",
  "opened": [],
  "chars": 0,
  "reached": false,
  "correct": true
 },
 {
  "id": "pymatgen#13",
  "skill": "pymatgen",
  "cond": "none",
  "answer": "Use pymatgen: `asf = AdsorbateSiteFinder(slab); adsorbed_slab = asf.add_adsorbate(O, site)`, where `site` is the chosen on-top coordinate from `find_adsorption_sites()`. This places the O Molecule at that site and returns the adsorbed Slab.",
  "opened": [],
  "chars": 0,
  "reached": false,
  "correct": true
 },
